---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<Layout title="Security" description="How Tor Browser Installer verifies downloads and what it does not hide.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow"><Icon name="shield" size={14} /> Security</span>
      <h1>What gets checked, and what you should know.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Installing Tor Browser is security-sensitive. This page explains exactly what 
        this tool verifies and what it deliberately does not attempt to hide.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout--warn">
        <Icon name="cross" size={20} />
        <div>
          <h4>This is not a Tor connection.</h4>
          <p>
            The installer downloads Tor Browser over <strong>plain HTTPS</strong>, not 
            over the Tor network. Anyone between you and the Tor Project's servers can 
            see that you fetched Tor Browser. They cannot see what you do inside it afterward.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 48px;">Verification process</h2>
      <ol class="verify-list">
        <li>
          <strong>SHA-256 checksum.</strong> The downloaded file's hash is computed locally 
          and compared against the value from the Tor Project's release JSON. A mismatch 
          stops the install immediately. The file is discarded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PGP signature.</strong> The detached <code>.asc</code> signature is 
          downloaded alongside the release and verified against the Tor Browser 
          Developers signing key using <code>sequoia-openpgp</code>. The key is fetched 
          at verification time from <code>keys.openpgp.org</code>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="fingerprint-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tor Browser Developers key fingerprint</span>
        <p class="mono fingerprint">EF6E 286D DA85 EA2A 4BA7&nbsp;DE68 4E2C 6E87 9329 8290</p>
        <p style="margin:0; font-size:0.86rem; color:var(--app-text-secondary);">
          Compare this against the fingerprint on
          <a href="https://support.torproject.org/tbb/how-to-verify-signature/">the Tor Project's verification guide</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:16px;">
        All verification happens <strong>before</strong> installation. If either check 
        fails, nothing is copied, extracted, or installed. No partial state is left behind.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">System-wide installs</h2>
      <p>
        Installing for all users requires writing to system-owned locations: 
        <code>/Applications</code> on macOS, <code>/opt</code> on Linux. Rather than 
        discovering a permission failure mid-install, the app asks for your password 
        up front and runs the entire install as one authenticated command.
      </p>
      <p>
        On macOS, a per-user install tries a plain copy first, and only escalates to 
        the Touch ID/password prompt if that copy is refused.
      </p>
      <p>
        The password is kept only in memory, sent once to the background worker thread 
        when the install starts, and is never written to the command log or disk.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">Known limitation</h2>
      <p>
        Earlier versions of this codebase shipped with checksum-only verification. 
        If you're auditing a build, confirm the binary actually performs PGP signature 
        verification (search for <code>verify_pgp_signature</code> in <code>install.rs</code>) 
        rather than assuming from this page alone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .callout {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .callout--warn {
    background: rgba(200, 45, 60, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(200, 45, 60, 0.25);
    color: var(--app-error);
  }
  .callout--warn h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--app-error); }
  .callout--warn p { margin: 0; color: #7a2129; font-size: 0.94rem; }
  .verify-list { display: grid; gap: 14px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .fingerprint-card {
    margin-top: 28px;
    background: var(--app-purple-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--app-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 20px 22px;
  }
  .fingerprint {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
  }
</style>
